                <pb facs="0238" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/3488: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stafford</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-17T12:00:00-04:00">September 17,
                        1931—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>32. Your No. 59 September 15th, 9 P.M. Dunn discussed situation fully with
                    Department and with legal counsel in New York. Senate amendment you mention will
                    probably be superseded by plan which Dunn is taking back to Santo Domingo
                    sailing today. Default of some sort is probably inevitable. Department
                    endeavoring to limit default and protect bondholders. Procedure still under
                    discussion. Schoenfeld will arrive Santo Domingo October 1st with full
                    instructions and knowledge of Department’s views.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
